---
layout: base.njk
title: "Daily install reports: what installed and what broke in AI agents"
permalink: /reports/
desc: "Free daily report from SkillMaxx's nightly sandbox run: how many agent skills, plugins and MCP servers installed in Claude Code, Codex, Grok Build, Cursor and Pi, what newly broke, what got fixed."
---
{% set nlid = "newsletter-top" %}{% set nlh = "Get the weekly scorecard" %}{% set nlp = "Daily reports live on the site only, we never email them. The free weekly email (Tuesdays) has the week's install scorecard plus new tools." %}
<div class="wrap prose"><h1 class="ph">Daily install reports</h1>
<p class="answer">Every night we really install every listed agent add-on in each agent that supports it and publish the result here.{% if reports.length %} Latest: <a href="/reports/{{ reports[0].date }}/">{{ reports[0].date }}</a>, {{ reports[0].pass }}/{{ reports[0].total }} installs passed.{% endif %}</p></div>
{% include "nlembed.njk" %}
<div class="wrap prose"><div class="tw"><table class="matrix"><thead><tr><th>Date</th><th>Add-ons</th><th>Installs passed</th><th>Needs a key</th><th>Confirmed broke</th><th>Really fixed</th><th>Flaky</th><th>New</th></tr></thead><tbody>
{% for r in reports %}<tr><th scope="row"><a href="/reports/{{ r.date }}/">{{ r.date }}</a>{% if r.baseline_change %} <span class="muted">(new baseline)</span>{% endif %}</th><td>{{ r.addons }}</td><td class="tok">{{ r.pass }}/{{ r.total }}</td><td>{{ r.needs_key }}</td><td>{{ r.broke.length if r.broke else "–" }}</td><td>{{ r.fixed.length if r.fixed else "–" }}</td><td>{{ r.flaky_list.length if r.flaky_list else "–" }}</td><td>{{ r.added.length if r.added else "–" }}</td></tr>{% endfor %}</tbody></table></div>
{% if runNotes.baselines.length and (reports | selectattr("baseline_change") | length) %}<div class="callout" role="note">{% for b in runNotes.baselines %}<p><b>New test baseline from {{ b.start }}.</b> {{ b.why }} ({% for a in site.agents %}{% if b.to[a] %}{{ a|agentName }} {{ b.from[a] }} → {{ b.to[a] }}{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endif %}{% endfor %}.) Scores before and after that date are not like-for-like. <a href="/reports/{{ b.start }}/">Details</a></p>{% endfor %}</div>{% endif %}
{% if runNotes.no_valid_run.length %}<h2 id="no-valid-run">No valid run</h2><p>We don't publish numbers from a run we know is wrong. These nights ran, but a bug in our own test harness broke the results, so there is no report for them:</p><ul>{% for n in runNotes.no_valid_run %}<li><b>{{ n.date }}</b>: {{ n.why }}</li>{% endfor %}</ul>{% endif %}
<p class="muted">"–" means there was no earlier run to compare with. Missed nights are not backfilled. Daily pages are an archive; for the current answer use <a href="/reports/latest/">today's report</a>, and for the big picture the <a href="/reports/week/">weekly scorecards</a>. <a href="/how-we-test/">How we test</a></p></div>
